# Hook scripts have no extension, so git decides their type by content and the
# editor decides their line endings by this rule. Without it `core.autocrlf`
# writes CRLF and the shebang becomes `env: bash\r`, at which point no hook runs
# at all and the tree looks guarded while nothing is.
Documentation/Hook/** text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
* text=auto eol=lf
